  "question": {
    "text": "If the maximum area bounded by <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math> and the line <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8704;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> square units, then the smallest prime number greater than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></math> is"
  },
